{"chunk_id":"4466bd","wall_time_seconds":0.9612486,"exit_code":1,"original_token_count":759,"output":"{"body":"Fixed in source by PR #174 (merge commit `c17a8cae`), merged into `dev`. Acceptance status:\n\n- **A due scheduled automation starts at its next tick while another automation's scheduled run is in progress.** Met.\n  The scheduler lease now covers one scan and is released before any run starts, so the next tick scans and starts\n  other due automations. The case \"a due automation starts at the next tick while another automation's scheduled run\n  is in progress\" failed on dev and passes. On a built app, with one automation's model call held for four minutes,\n  the other automation ran each minute.\n- **Two processes that share a database still never sweep at the same time, and one automation still never runs twice\n  at once.** Met, with \"sweep\" read as the scan. Two processes never scan at the same time, which the case \"two\n  processes on one database never scan at the same time\" shows. A sweep now spans the runs it started, so sweeps\n  overlap while runs execute. Each scheduled run and Run now holds a run lease of its own until its outcome is written,\n  and the stale reset and the paired-host reconcile act only after taking that lease, so no tick resets, reconciles, or\n  restarts a run that is still going.\n- **LAST CHECKED keeps advancing about once a minute during a long run.** Met. Every tick writes its check, and the\n  built-app journey read a new LAST CHECKED value each minute while the long run was held.\n- **A test runs two automations, one with a long run, and shows the second starting on time.** Met, the case above.\n\nNot covered here, and still open: #138, #140 (after a hard kill only the killed automation now waits), and #141. No\npackaged or Windows run was made for this change.\n","createdAt":"2026-10-02T22:35:42Z"}
