Handoff for the existing Codex owner of #138, identified in [the ownership comment](https://github.com/vivary-dev/vivary/issues/138#issuecomment-5961876359): please take this scoped correction through the existing Zo workflow, review, required validation, and merge into dev once the gates pass. Please reply here when you pick it up. Preserve the other owner's files and coordinate the requested separate fix branch with the current PR branch.

Rechecked at 01:16 UTC: #173 is still open at `5ce5468c95f3858dce712b89fb4fa135f916fb45`, with no newer fix. [The Windows fallback finding](https://github.com/vivary-dev/vivary/pull/173#discussion_r4170897427) reproduces. Exiting the server after cleanup rejection cancels the parent's live-PID-only tree fallback. Merely omitting exit is insufficient because IPC and HTTP can already be closed.

Minimal proposed production patch against that head:

```diff
--- a/packages/workbench/server/plugins/02-local-code-lifecycle.ts
+++ b/packages/workbench/server/plugins/02-local-code-lifecycle.ts
@@ -26,17 +26,22 @@
 export default defineNitroPlugin(async (nitroApp) => {
   // guard:allow-env-credential - The dedicated CLI and desktop launchers own this process's exit.
   const standalone = process.env.VIVARY_STANDALONE_HOST === "1";
+  // guard:allow-env-credential - The Windows desktop parent needs a live PID for its tree fallback.
+  const keepWindowsTreeAlive = standalone && process.platform === "win32"
+    && process.env.VIVARY_DESKTOP_HOST === "1";
   let stopping = false;
   const shutdown = () => {
     if (stopping) return;
     stopping = true;
+    // IPC and HTTP may close before cleanup settles; taskkill needs a live tree root.
+    if (keepWindowsTreeAlive) setInterval(() => {}, 1_000);
     const cleanup = stopLocalWork().then(() =>
       standalone ? nitroApp.hooks.callHook("close") : undefined);
     void cleanup.then(() => {
       if (standalone) process.exit(0);
     }).catch(() => {
       console.error("[vivary-local-host] Shutdown did not settle.");
-      if (standalone) process.exit(1);
+      if (standalone && !keepWindowsTreeAlive) process.exit(1);
     });
   };
   const removeSignalHandlers = () => {
```

Extend `packages/workbench/tests/desktop-server-shutdown.test.mjs` with Windows success, pending cleanup, preview rejection, Nitro-close rejection, and standalone-without-desktop failure controls. In pending/error cases, clear the fixture's keepAlive interval and let IPC close before asserting that the server stays alive until the parent force-kills it. Select the simulated platform only while initializing the already-imported lifecycle, then restore it so tsx loading is unaffected. Preserve the existing shutdown, disconnect, POSIX failure, and hosted controls.

Diagnostic evidence: the current source failed the three Windows pending/error cases; this proposal passed all nine cases. Removing the referenced hold reproduced those same three failures. This used Linux Node 24's built-in TypeScript loading with controlled dependencies, not the pinned tsx runner or a Windows package. Independent technical review found no blocking issue in the proposed correction. It verified that pinned srvx closes HTTP without exiting, so the referenced hold is necessary. These results do not establish real Windows tree cleanup or replace the repository gates.

On Zo, run the official focused test command and applicable exact-head CI, review the built-server composition, and verify real Windows preview-descendant cleanup plus normal quit timing and automation persistence. Keep the parent's PID guard, 15-second fallback, cleanup ordering, and non-Windows/CLI exit behavior unchanged. Correct the unconditional failure-exit wording in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `packages/desktop/README.md`, record the HLDD review, and regenerate the existing documentation mirrors. Preserve historical acceptance evidence.

The previous head had all ten checks green, including an Entire gate with one recorded approval. Recheck required review, CI, Entire approval/freshness, source mirroring, and packaged acceptance for the final head before merging. No source was pushed from the diagnostic environment. No publication, deployment, or promotion to main is requested.

